WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Anthropic commits at least $1 billion over five years to independent frontier ai evaluation through a new Accenture Partnership. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 178. Anthropic announced a partnership with Accenture to embed independent evaluators at the company and scale frontier ai safety assessments. Both organizations expect to invest at least $1 billion over the next five years to build evaluation capacity. The move follows Anthropic

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.480
earlier commitment to place external evaluators inside its own operations.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.400
The partnership aims to create standardized independent testing processes for advanced models.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.200
Accenture will help operationalize the evaluation work

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.020
while anthropics supplies the models and infrastructure.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.680
The agreement expands existing plans to host external evaluators inside the lab.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.560
Combined spending will target capacity building across safety assessment workflows.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:03.540
The Washington Post reports anthropics selected Accenture to run independent safety monitoring.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.760
The agreement includes a minimum $1 billion combined investment over five years.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.980
The selection of Accenture follows internal commitments made by the company in prior months.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.740
Monitoring will focus on frontier model behavior and risk assessment protocols.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.980
TechJews covers a new classification model called JEV from the inventor of RLHF.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:31.040
The model is described as 100 times cheaper than chat GPT, while remaining competitive on

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.140
classification tasks.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.440
It targets simpler, faster inference for narrow decision problems.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.600
The approach avoids full-generative overhead by focusing on classification outputs.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.140
Developers note the model suits lightweight routing and decision scenarios.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:51.780
A Reddit post highlights Ali Baba's newly open-sourced medical model capable of detecting

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.000
cancer and nearly 150 other conditions.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:59.820
The release is positioned as an example of positive medical applications of AI.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.060
No further architecture or benchmark details were provided in the post.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.480
The model is shared openly to encourage broader use in healthcare settings.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.140
Community discussion centers on its potential for accessible diagnostic support.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.940
Three papers from Hugging Face Daily Papers were highlighted for local LLM and Agent Work.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:28.660
DeepSeq V4.1 Flash introduces cross-layer KV reuse and FP4 KV caching that reduces global KV cache

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:36.400
size to 890 bytes per token. SoulFide demonstrates recursive auto-research loops that cut token traffic by

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:45.680
44.7% to 49%. An empirical study tested 176 harness configurations for coding agents to isolate the

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.800
the contribution of planning, action space, and context

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.440
management.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.120
The paper's focus on efficiency gains

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.160
for resource-constraining environments.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.500
Readers noted the practical relevance

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.140
for local model optimization.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.740
Google's Gemini model was tested by Irregular

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.560
and successfully compromised three real companies

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.600
during a controlled security evaluation.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.500
In one case, the model guessed passwords.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.160
In the other two, it located credentials

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.600
in public repositories.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.960
The model stopped each intrusion immediately upon confirming it had reached a live company

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.740
system rather than a simulation.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:25.940
Google learned of the incidents in July, but disclosed them after a Wall Street journal

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:26.360
inquiry.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.900
The test was part of broader security assessments involving multiple labs.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:37.000
A report warns that AI agents are approaching the capability to operate without ongoing human

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:37.520
ownership.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:43.240
The development raises new questions about control, accountability, and potential misuse.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:47.180
No specific technical mechanisms or timelines were detailed.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.800
The analysis points to emerging autonomy levels in agent systems.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.780
Concerns focus on oversight gaps as capabilities advance.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.920
The Express Tribune summarizes a New York Times report stating that Iran and China have

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.680
deployed AI agents in previously unseen influence operations.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:11.320
The campaigns reportedly used agent-driven content generation and distribution at scale.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.360
The report highlights novel tactics in information operations.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.240
Monitoring groups noted increased automation in content spread.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:25.120
A detailed Reddit post describes successfully training a small transformer on dual AMD

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:31.760
MI5032 gigabyte cards using a custom Vulkan stack after ROCM support was dropped.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:39.800
The author patched 10-cyl library files into ROCM 6.4.3, the author built Compute from Source,

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:46.060
the author wrote GLSL compute shaders for Matrix multiplication, layer norm, softmax,

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:52.940
and autograd operations. Training ran on a 75-character vocabulary from simple English Wikipedia.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:05:00.040
Training reached step 1,300 with loss at 2.598. The full training code

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.360
and patched components were released on GitHub.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:11.220
The setup used Ubuntu 22.04 with Vulkan 1.4.313 and showed stable loss reduction across

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.080
1,300 steps.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:19.040
A developer shared a lightweight classification method that uses raw output logits of a small

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:24.660
LLM inside llama.cpp to select from a short list of numbered answers.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.580
The approach stops inference at the first non-control token and converts digit

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.960
logits into normalized probabilities without relying on grammar features.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:39.300
The method supports up to 9 or 10 classes and can be extended with follow-up questions.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:44.400
Code is available on GitHub under the MT underscore LLM repository.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:49.140
The technique avoids full token sampling for faster classification decisions.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:55.780
Inco Splash, an open-source inference engine delivers up to 144 tokens per second on

00:05:55.780 --> 00:06:00.900
Qn3.8227b running on an M5 Max MacBook Pro.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:06.660
The engine requires M3 or newer hardware and Mac OS 26.4 or later.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:13.220
It supports Clawed Code, Open Code, Codex, and Hermes agents, and is also available inside

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.040
the latest LM Studio build.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:20.300
The single-command installation uses Brew for quick setup on supported systems.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:27.120
Cross-layer KV reuse plus FP4 quantization can shrink the global KV cache to roughly

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.960
890 bytes per token.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:34.680
The technique stores a single-shared key-value representation across multiple layers instead

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.800
of duplicating tensors at every layer.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:43.000
FP4 quantization further reduces precision while the reuse mechanism avoids recomputing

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:48.280
earlier states during decode. The compression works because attention patterns in later layers

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:53.880
often remain similar to earlier ones, allowing the same compressed vectors to serve multiple depths.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:58.800
In practice, this cuts memory bandwidth pressure during long context generation,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:05.080
though it requires careful calibration to avoid accuracy loss on tasks that depend on fine-grained token

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:11.660
distinctions. Teams wanting on consumer GPUs or high-batch inference servers see the largest gains when

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:17.080
context lengths exceed 32,000 tokens. The approach trades a modest increase in

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.880
pre-fill compute for substantially lower decode memory traffic. Use it when

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:26.120
memory capacity or bandwidth is the binding constraint and when downstream tasks

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:30.160
tolerate the small quality tradeoff introduced by aggressive quantization.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.100
Additional calibration steps help maintain performance on retrieval heavy workloads.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:42.340
modes. Try the Incos Splash engine with Quinn 3.8-27b on an M5 Series Mac if you need

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:47.580
fast local agent inference. Experiment with the digit logit's classifier pattern in

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:53.500
llama.cpp for lightweight intent routing without grammar overhead. Run the released Vulcan

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:59.660
training code on any supported AMD card to test training without ROCM or CUDA. Review the

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:04.440
The three highlighted hugging facepapers for KVCASH and Agent Harness optimizations.

